{"type":"message","id":"240338ee","parentId":"e503765e","timestamp":"2026-03-17T18:24:52.226Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] Yes — using your **manual fixed request**, the endpoint **does return those extra fields**.\n\nI manually POSTed your payload to:\n- `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n\nand in the returned raw response, these fields are present:\n- `confidence_interpretation`\n- `recommended_next_steps`\n- `references`\n- `summary`\n- `visual_evidence`\n\nSo the result is:\n\n- **Pipeline script / previous runs:** those fields were **not** in the actual response\n- **Manual fixed request you provided:** those fields **are** in the actual response\n\nThat means the issue is **not the endpoint in general** — it’s that the earlier request payload being sent by the pipeline was **different** from this fixed manual payload.\n\nI saved both files in the workspace:\n- Request used manually: `manual_kidney_fixed_request.json`\n- Raw manual endpoint response: `manual_kidney_manual_endpoint_response_2026-03-17T18-22-manual.json`\n\nMost likely cause: the earlier pipeline used a different prototype/request structure — in particular, it was hitting a payload where the nested analyzer endpoint/path and/or prototype content differed, so the X-AI tracking parameters stayed empty. If you want, I can now compare the **manual working payload** against the **pipeline-generated payload** and pinpoint the exact differences causing the missing fields.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_012ee6229829f48d0169b99c6e312c8191b5d01388f9927e2a\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":158,"output":300,"cacheRead":67840,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":68298,"cost":{"input":0.000395,"output":0.0045000000000000005,"cacheRead":0.01696,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.021855}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":17737